Third-party components
----------------------

migkit drives external programs rather than reimplementing them. They are not
bundled or redistributed here - migkit invokes them when present, or pins them
in a generated docker-compose file that pulls the published image at run time.
Each remains under its own licence, held by its own authors.

Invoked as local programs when installed:
  pg_dump, pg_restore, psql            PostgreSQL Global Development Group
  mydumper, myloader                   MySQL Data Dumper project
  pgloader                             Dimitri Fontaine
  mongodump, mongorestore, mongosh     MongoDB, Inc.
  atlas                                Ariga
  liquibase                            Liquibase
  reladiff, datacompy, sqlglot, migra  respective authors

Pulled as container images by the generated streaming pipeline
(migkit/movers.py, stream_codegen):
  Debezium Connect      Apache License 2.0   https://debezium.io
  Redpanda              Business Source Licence / Redpanda Community Licence
                                             https://redpanda.com

The streaming pipeline is an internal implementation detail: it is selected by
migkit, not by the operator, and the command surface does not expose it. This
file exists so the components are still credited and their licences traceable.
